Cross-module selector interpolation in [%styled.global].

The PPX cannot resolve M's classes at PPX time (M compiles separately),
so it emits NUL-delimited sentinels in the extracted [@@@css] strings
plus a [@@@css.refs ...] descriptor and a synthetic `let _ = M.x` for
ocamldep tracking. The aggregator extracts the index from M's post-PPX
file and substitutes the sentinels with the referenced binding's identity
class.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml m.re > m.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl m.ml -o m.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml n.re > n.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl n.ml -o n.ml

The post-PPX `n.ml` carries unresolved sentinels in [@@@css ...] and the
synthetic dep markers. The styled.global module shell is preserved.

  $ cat n.ml
  [@@@css "body .\000M.marker\000{color:red;}"]
  [@@@css ".\000M.card\000:hover{cursor:pointer;}"]
  [@@@css.refs [("M.marker", "n.ml", 4, 10, 18); ("M.card", "n.ml", 8, 5, 11)]]
  let _ = M.marker
  let _ = M.card
  module Globals =
    struct
      let to_string () = ""
      let makeProps ?key () = Js.Obj.empty ()[@@warning "-27-32"]
      let make _props = CSS.global_style_tag (to_string ())
    end

The aggregator resolves each reference to the identity class of the
referenced binding. `M.marker` becomes `._id_12qpfnx` and `M.card`
becomes `._id_v2n2gu`, so `.$(M.card):hover` becomes
`._id_v2n2gu:hover`. One identity class stands for the whole binding,
whatever its number of atoms.

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml n.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  body ._id_12qpfnx{color:red;}
  ._id_v2n2gu:hover{cursor:pointer;}
  ._a_5r08qs,._t1_5r08qs._t1_5r08qs,._t2_5r08qs._t2_5r08qs._t2_5r08qs{display:flex;}
  ._a_9432ej,._t1_9432ej._t1_9432ej,._t2_9432ej._t2_9432ej._t2_9432ej{padding:10px;}
